# Using Elixir Registries to name processes

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:obsidian_livebook, path: "/home/scossar/projects/elixir/obsidian_livebook"}
])
```

## About Registries

`Registry` is the Elixir process registry module. It makes it possible to use any Elixir value to name a process, (as opposed to only being able to use atoms to name processes).

Docs:

* [Local, decentralized, scalable registry](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/supervisor-and-application.html#local-decentralized-and-scalable-registry)
* [Elixir docs: Registry](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/Registry.html)

## Register and access named processes

```elixir
Registry.start_link(name: KV, keys: :unique)
```

Instead of passing an atom to the `name` option, pass a tuple with the shape `{:via, registry_module, {registry_name, process_name}}`:

```elixir
counter = {:via, Registry, {KV, "counter"}}
{:ok, _} = Agent.start_link(fn -> 0 end, name: counter)
```

```elixir
Agent.update(counter, & &1 + 1)
```

```elixir
Agent.get(counter, & &1)
```

## Publish to Obsidian

```elixir
ObsidianLivebook.publish("/home/scossar/obsidian_vault", __ENV__.file)
```
